so I just filmed this whole 20 minute  review of the Samsung S 20 altra out of  focus  what's going on guys my name is David  Tomich and welcome back to the channel  today we're talking about the s20 ultra  and my experience over the last three  months the fact that I'm starting this  video with an out-of-focus complaint is  the very reason why I'm making this  video so today we're gonna be talking  about my personal experience using this  as my daily driver from everything from  the display all the way down to the  battery quality how I found it to be in  a day to day situation and all the  little bits and pieces that I found not  worth the 2000 Australian dollar price  it cost today in 2020 so first of all  let's talk about the display and start  on a positive note the display is  phenomenal the 120 Hertz refresh rate  the color clarity the sharpness  everything about this screen is so  appealing to the eye it is by far the  best screen I've ever seen on a  smartphone  now I'm no mkbhd and I haven't seen  every single smartphone on the market so  I can't say it's the best in the world  but it is definitely the best I've seen  in my personal life time as most of you  are probably aware you can't use 120  Hertz on this device at its highest  setting Samsung just doesn't allow you  unfortunately it says that it drains the  battery too fast but I personally would  have liked to see that option as just a  yep okay whatever that's my fault  and my risk if I lose 50 cent battery in  half a day instead of only using 10% but  that might come in a later software  update so let's stay tuned and keep our  fingers crossed unlocking this phone has  actually been quite a pleasure having  the under glass fingerprint reader in  conjunction with the face unlock has  made it very simple to unlock this phone  at any given time having the position of  the under fingerprint reader as such a  small central location probably isn't  the best I would have liked to see it a  little bit better and it didn't take me  about a week to get used to the position  but after that time I really was able to  unlock this phone very fluidly almost  9% of the time with either the  fingerprint scanner or the face unlock  it's very rare that I have to use the  password anymore so that is definitely a  good feature and something I'd like to  see continuously improved so that after  a little bit of time we don't really  even have to touch it properly to unlock  the phone but when we do unlock the  phone and open up a camera app you're  probably going to see the same issues I  experienced today and every other day I  record a YouTube video the s20 ultra has  such a huge sensor in such a small  device that its depth of field isn't  perfect and it's focusing in 4k  especially video recording mode is  average of s what you'll find because  that's what I found and many many other  users have found as well is the fact  that it can't focus very well on  close-up subjects or faraway subjects in  4k or ake a video recording it doesn't  have auto face tracking it doesn't have  auto subject tracking so if I was to  move around violently in this video it  wouldn't stay in focus I don't want to  because of the very simple fact that  I've just managed to get it in focus  again so if I move too much and get it  out of focus well then it's gonna take  me 20 minutes to bring it back into  focus and get it right for you guys as  it is I'm already using an iPad with the  screen mirrored so I can actually keep  an eye on it because I'm so sick of  repeating myself a hundred times over to  make sure everything's in focus even  when we're talking about photography of  small objects or up-close objects the  main 108 megapixel sensor camera is not  the best it tends to produce depth of  field and bokeh way way too early in the  object and it blurs out maybe from here  backwards instead of all the way back or  for example my ears could be completely  blurred out and the front of my face in  focus so it is having trouble finding  focus and there have been some updates  which have made it better but it still  isn't perfect which makes me a little  bit cautious and a little bit worried  that the simple fact is this is a  hardware problem and not a software  problem  the Elektra wide camera which is  definitely one of  most used and favorite pieces of  hardware on this device is only 12  megapixels it isn't the best camera in  the world it isn't the worst camera in  the world it produces very high-end  quality images but not as high-end as  the main camera I would have liked to  see a much higher speck in the ultra  wide because that's something I  personally use a lot I feel like a lot  of people like the ultra wide because it  gives it the more natural more realistic  interpretation of the world but hey  maybe the next s20 series will see that  in and the zoom camera well I'm hoping  that you've seen my last video on the  SpaceX zoom comparison it's pretty good  up to about 30 times zoom anything over  30 times zoom starts to get very blurry  very noisy and kind of unusable by the  time you get to a hundred times ooh so  it's a nice feature to have it's a nice  gimmick to show off to people but that's  about it you can't really get the best  quality images out of it  unless you have a tripod unless you have  perfect conditions unless there's no  wind and blah blah blah it's really a  gimmick at the end of the day and  something that has sold this phone to  many people so props to Samsung for  trying to get innovative technology into  phones so early but at the same time I  wish they would have waited a year or  two before they brought out this  technology before it wasn't absolutely  perfect if you're unaware this phone is  also capable of recording in 8k now I  record all my YouTube views in 4k not 8k  not 1080p not anything else  why because it seems like this device is  optimized for 4k 1080p is very noisy and  very grainy 4k the colors just aren't  right there's something wrong with the  4k settings I don't know if it's just me  maybe it's just the environment I'm in  maybe it's the studio lighting and the  backlighting but 8k just doesn't work  properly in this situation in an outdoor  situations it's pretty good but I think  at the end of the day the 4k is the most  optimized on this device and is by far  the best for everyday you  something that really surprised me was  the speakers on this device I didn't  really expect them to be amazing but  combined with the screen the dual  speakers and the Dolby Atmos system  inside it's phenomenal  like the first time I watched a YouTube  video on this device  I was mesmerized I was blown away I was  immersed in that experience I'm not  usually like that on a tablet or a  smartphone I have a full home theater  with a surround sound system so I know  what good quality sound should be yes I  know that's ironic considering most of  my videos have terrible sound but we'll  just get past that point the speakers on  this device are actually really really  good  they're crystal clear they're really  loud at times and combined with a screen  like I said they make a really good  viewing experience the fact that the  battery on this device is also super  large makes it a great complementary  feature the fast charging was something  I never thought I'd use either but the  fact that I can forget to put my phone  on charge at nighttime leave it my  bedside table instead of on the opposite  side of the room because I turn my alarm  off and then just go straight back to  sleep if it's not means if I forget to  charge at night time in half an hour in  an hour it can be fully charged or 50%  charged that means I can go throughout  my whole day and still not drain this  battery to its absolute minimum if I'm  using this device pretty heavily on a  day phone calls videos photos everything  I don't think I usually want use more  than 50% which means in half an hour in  the morning I can get my phone to nearly  full very quickly without having to  worry about charging it overnight for  hours on end so what's my verdict on the  s20 ultra should you buy it should you  wait should you just skip it completely  well personally I think that it is a  very good device the 120 Hertz refresh  rate makes it something really  pleasurable to use every single day it  doesn't hurt your eyes as much as normal  devices do but if I think if you're  buying it for the purpose of the camera  it isn't there yet the focus and depth  of field problems are too much to shy  away from the fact that it's continuous  in everyone  videos and I have to re-record things  consistently is really frustrating and  really annoying now for me personally if  this was a day-to-day device it could be  anything but because it was a device  specifically purchased to replace my  DSLR it isn't everything so having said  that I think if the iPhone 12 comes out  with 120 Hertz refresh rate a USBC  charger and a really really good camera  combination on the back to take on this  monster it might be something worth  considering if you're in the same boat  looking at purchasing in s 20 or  potentially the iPhone 12 at the end of  the year definitely wait to see what the  comparison is going to be like but at  the moment with the software issues and  potentially the secret hardware issues I  don't think the s 20 is the perfect  photography videography camera I do  think it's a great device in general  there's absolutely nothing wrong with it  besides from some very picky pedantic  bits and pieces but overall it's a solid  9 out of 10 anyway that's all for me  today guys I hope you enjoyed the video  if you did make sure you smash that  subscribe button  20:20 style help me get to that 5k  subscriber mark and when we do I'll make  sure to do another big giveaway so until  then as always I'll see you next Monday
 

